      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic managed object storage task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file upload_object.py using AWS.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] upload_object.py - uploads a file or byte stream to managed object storage\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] presigned_download.py - creates a time-limited signed download URL for a stored object\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] object_metadata.py - reads object metadata or head information from managed object storage\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] list_prefix.py - lists stored objects under a bucket or container prefix\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] storage_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Managed Object Storage\n6. [HELPER] storage_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Managed Object Storage\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] stored_document_ocr.py - Run OCR on a stored document object\n8. [LATER-STEP] stored_text_translate.py - Translate text extracted from a stored document\n9. [LATER-STEP] stored_asset_summary.py - Summarize content extracted from a stored asset\n10. [LATER-STEP] asset_metadata_embedding.py - Embed object metadata and extracted text for search\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
